---
/* HeroIllustration.astro — cursor-scrubbed sprite-sheet portrait card.
   Overrides this repo's "one hero treatment" rule on record, by
   explicit instruction: this replaces (not adds to) the hero's
   signature interactive moment, it doesn't stack a second one.

   A small card beside the copy. A full-bleed backdrop (the figure
   filling nearly the whole banner, copy overlaid on a bottom-fade
   scrim) was tried by explicit instruction, matching a reference —
   and reverted, also by explicit instruction ("too big"), back to
   this. See git history for that version if it comes back; it also
   needed a ThemeRail.astro mobile-position fix (the vertically
   centred toggle collided with the copy once the copy sat lower in
   the band) that's irrelevant again now the copy is back in its
   original spot, but harmless to leave in place.

   Pointer position over the hero band maps to a frame index — mostly the
   pointer's x, with a small y contribution so vertical movement is
   felt too — and a canvas draws just that frame's slice out of the
   sprite each tick. The index is damped with a lerp rather than
   snapped straight to the target, so the motion reads as tracking
   rather than flipping; leaving the card eases the index back to 0
   (the clip's rest pose) the same way.

   public/images/hero-sprite.webp is a GRID of 48 frames (700x980 each,
   8 columns x 6 rows) — every 4th frame of the 8s, 24fps source clip
   (a watercolour version of the character on a near-white backdrop,
   1080x1920, added 2026-09-29).

   Each frame is cropped to the character before export: source window
   x 40-1080, y 374-1830 (the figure's union bounds across all 48 frames,
   x 56-1069, y 390-1812, plus a margin), which is 5:7 — the box's
   --hero-art-ratio (tokens.css). The box's edges are the figure's edges,
   so bottom-aligning it puts the chair legs on the CTA row's line.
   AskBubble's launcher position is measured in this same 700x980 frame.

   Export: scripts/hero-sprite.py, from the source clip. The source
   backdrop is off-white (247-253, never pure); the script lifts only
   the highlights so it becomes exactly white, mattes with a soft ramp
   (alpha 0 at white to 1 at 40 levels below), and then, near the edge
   and only where the art around it is dark, un-mixes the white from
   the palest strands so her hair doesn't wear a pale cut-out outline
   on the dark page. No flood fill, so the watercolour edges stay soft.
   (mix-blend-mode: multiply on an opaque sprite was tried first and is
   smaller, but any fading ancestor — the Reveal wrapper — isolates the
   blend and flashes a white box on load. Colour-to-alpha against white
   was exact but 12-15MB.)

   public/images/hero-idle.webp (frame 0) is what non-JS, reduced-motion
   and coarse-pointer visitors see.

   Frame size tracks display size (~2x the 31rem box height) rather than
   the source's full resolution — nearest-neighbour sampling (below)
   keeps the grid from bleeding colour across cell edges, and it looks
   pixelated when upscaled, so resolution is matched, not maximised.

   Fine pointers only. Touch/coarse pointers and `prefers-reduced-motion`
   get hero-idle.webp (frame 0) drawn once into the same canvas, with no
   pointer tracking; the <img> is the fallback if the canvas fails.

   Night light (dark mode; NIGHT LIGHT in tokens.css): after each frame
   is drawn, three layers are painted on a second canvas, clipped to her
   shape with her frame's alpha, and blended on — a multiply shade that
   darkens everything the screen doesn't reach, the screen's cool light
   (soft-light) on her chest, chin, lower face and keyboard hand, and a
   faint screen-blend glow on her face. The face lights move with her
   head via FACE_DX/FACE_DY (measured per frame off the sprite; re-measure
   if the sprite is re-exported). All of it is scaled by `lit`, which
   eases between 0 (light mode, nothing drawn) and 1 (dark) over
   --dur-night when the theme changes, so the lights come on rather than
   snapping; instant under reduced motion. The canvas only repaints when
   the frame, the size or the theme changes, or during that fade.

   Sync: every time the drawn frame changes, the figure dispatches a
   bubbling `hero-scrub:frame` event ({ frame, count }). AskBubble's Moss
   listens and shows the same frame of his own 48-frame clip, so the two
   characters share one timeline and one damping loop and can't drift.
   The pointer is read over the whole band the figure sits in (the
   hero section, via its data-themeband), and its x/y across that band
   picks the frame: she responds as soon as the cursor is anywhere in the
   hero, and Moss, being inside the band, never counts as leaving it.
   Leaving the band eases her back to frame 0.

   The cursor lamp (dark mode; CursorLamp.astro announces where it is
   with a `cursor-lamp` event). The hero row sits above the page's
   screen-blended lamp, so the lamp lights the ground behind her and
   she is lit here instead, from the frame on screen (values under
   CURSOR LAMP in tokens.css):
     - colour x light: a light map of the lamp, multiplied by her
       colours and added, so dark hair stays dark and the red gets
       richer. (Screening the lamp over her fogged her: it lifts the
       darks most.)
     - form shade: her side away from the lamp dims a little.
     - rim: the strip of her edge facing the lamp, lit by its pool, so
       the edge catches the light and travels round her as it moves.
     - glint: a faint highlight on the laptop lid, sliding with it.
   And on a second canvas behind her, reaching past her box: contact
   pools under the legs and slippers (all night, lamp or not), and the
   lamp's light on the floor around her with her shadow cut out of it,
   skewed away from the lamp and longer the lower it is — a shadow is
   light that didn't arrive, and the page lamp alone is too faint on
   this ground to show one. All of it scales with `lit` and the lamp's falloff.
   Chosen on request from the round-2 mocks. The sprite was re-exported
   with its white edge un-mixed for the dark page: scripts/hero-sprite.py. */
interface Props {
  alt: string;
  size?: number;
}
const { alt, size = 480 } = Astro.props;
---
<figure class="hero-scrub" style={`--size:${size}px`} tabindex="0">
  <canvas class="hero-scrub__ground" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
  <canvas class="hero-scrub__canvas" aria-label={alt} role="img"></canvas>
  <img class="hero-scrub__still" src="/images/hero-idle.webp" alt={alt} />
</figure>

<style>
  .hero-scrub {
    position: relative;
    margin: 0;
    flex: none;
    /* Sized by height (--hero-art-h, tokens.css) so the figure matches
       the hero's copy stack beside it; the cropped aspect sets the
       width. max-width: 100% lets it give way when the row is short on
       room (the copy column never does) — as max-width, not inside the
       min(): a percentage there resolves to 0 while the parent is sizing
       to its content, and the figure collapses. --size still caps it for
       a caller that passes a smaller one. The long history of vw-based
       widths this replaced is in git. */
    width: min(calc(var(--hero-art-h) * var(--hero-art-ratio)), var(--size));
    max-width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: var(--hero-art-ratio);
    line-height: 0;
    outline: none;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  /* Her floor shadow and contact pools: behind her, reaching past her
     box sideways (the shadow swings away from the lamp), above her head
     and a little below her feet, so the light drawn here has room to
     fade out before any edge. */
  .hero-scrub__ground {
    position: absolute;
    left: -60%; right: -60%; top: -35%; bottom: -8%;
    width: 220%; height: 143%;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .hero-scrub:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 6px; }

  .hero-scrub__canvas {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }
  /* The still is frame 0, already cropped to the same window. */
  .hero-scrub__still {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }


  /* Default (JS-driven) state: canvas visible, static fallback hidden.
     .no-js-scrub (set by the script below only when scrubbing can't
     run — coarse pointer or reduced motion) flips this so the single
     still frame shows instead and the canvas is inert. */
  .hero-scrub__still { display: none; }
  .hero-scrub.no-js-scrub .hero-scrub__canvas { display: none; }
  .hero-scrub.no-js-scrub .hero-scrub__still { display: block; }
</style>

<script>
  const FRAME_COUNT = 48;
  const FRAME_W = 700;
  const FRAME_H = 980;
  // Frames are exported pre-cropped to the character (see the header
  // comment), so the whole frame is drawn.
  const CROP_X = 0;
  const CROP_Y = 0;
  const CROP_W = FRAME_W;
  const CROP_H = FRAME_H;
  const COLS = 8;
  const SMOOTHING = 0.14; // higher = snappier, lower = more inertia
  const Y_INFLUENCE = 0.28; // how much vertical pointer position nudges the frame vs x

  // Night light (dark mode). Where her face sits in each frame, as an
  // offset from frame 0 in % of the frame, measured off the sprite (the
  // centroid of her skin tones in the head band): x 38-47%, y 20-22%.
  // The face light moves by this so it stays on her as she turns.
  const FACE_DX = [0,0,.2,0,.1,.1,-.1,-1.3,-2.3,-2.6,-2.6,-2.7,-2.7,-2.7,-2.8,-4.2,-6.6,-7.6,-7.8,-7.9,-7.8,-7.4,-4.4,-.9,.2,.3,.1,.3,.2,.2,.2,.2,.4,.8,1,.9,1,.9,.7,.3,.1,0,.1,0,.1,0,.1,.1];
  const FACE_DY = [0,-.1,-.2,-.3,-.5,-.5,-.6,-.8,-.7,-.7,-.6,-.7,-.7,-.7,-.7,-1.3,-1.5,-1.7,-1.5,-1.4,-1.3,-1.3,-1.1,-.1,-.1,-.7,-1,-1,-.9,-1,-.9,-1,-.9,-.6,.2,.3,.4,.3,0,-.1,-.4,-.4,-.4,-.5,-.5,-.4,-.4,-.5];

  // One elliptical light: centre and radii in % of the frame (as CSS
  // radial-gradient(rx ry at cx cy)), from `inner` alpha at the centre
  // to `outer` at the rim and beyond.
  type Ellipse = { cx: number; cy: number; rx: number; ry: number; inner: number; outer: number; hold?: number };

  type Night = { screen: string; shade: string; screenK: number; glowK: number; shadeK: number; on: number; ms: number };
  const readNight = (): Night => {
    const cs = getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
    const num = (n: string) => parseFloat(cs.getPropertyValue(n)) || 0;
    return {
      screen: cs.getPropertyValue('--hero-screen').trim(),
      shade: cs.getPropertyValue('--hero-shade').trim(),
      screenK: num('--hero-screen-k'),
      glowK: num('--hero-glow-k'),
      shadeK: num('--hero-shade-k'),
      on: num('--hero-night'),   // 0 light, 1 dark
      ms: num('--dur-night'),    // "900ms" → 900
    };
  };
  // The lamp on her (CURSOR LAMP in tokens.css).
  type LampK = { gain: number; sat: number; lift: number; rimK: number; rimW: number; formK: number; glintK: number; floorK: number; castK: number; contactK: number; hue: string; reach: number };
  const readLampK = (): LampK => {
    const cs = getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
    const num = (n: string) => parseFloat(cs.getPropertyValue(n)) || 0;
    const hue = cs.getPropertyValue('--lamp-hue').trim().match(/[\d.]+/g)?.slice(0, 3).join(' ') ?? '255 214 170';
    return {
      gain: num('--hero-lamp-gain'), sat: num('--hero-lamp-sat'), lift: num('--hero-lamp-lift'), rimK: num('--hero-rim-k'), rimW: num('--hero-rim-w'),
      formK: num('--hero-form-k'), glintK: num('--hero-glint-k'),
      floorK: num('--hero-floor-k'), castK: num('--hero-cast-k'), contactK: num('--hero-contact-k'),
      hue, reach: (num('--lamp-reach') || 70) / 100,
    };
  };
  // The page lamp's falloff (CursorLamp.astro's gradient stops), as
  // fractions of its reach.
  const FALLOFF: [number, number][] = [[0, 1], [0.25, 0.7], [0.5, 0.35], [0.75, 0.12], [1, 0]];
  const falloffAt = (t: number) => {
    for (let i = 1; i < FALLOFF.length; i++) if (t <= FALLOFF[i][0]) {
      const [a0, v0] = FALLOFF[i - 1], [a1, v1] = FALLOFF[i];
      return v0 + (v1 - v0) * (t - a0) / (a1 - a0);
    }
    return 0;
  };
  const pool = (c: CanvasRenderingContext2D, x: number, y: number, reach: number, rgb: string, a: number) => {
    const g = c.createRadialGradient(x, y, 0, x, y, Math.max(1, reach));
    for (const [t, v] of FALLOFF) g.addColorStop(t, `rgb(${rgb} / ${Math.min(1, a * v)})`);
    return g;
  };
  // The laptop lid in the 700x980 frame (it doesn't move across frames).
  const LID: [number, number][] = [[250, 377], [492, 377], [473, 515], [220, 515]];

  // Close to the sitewide --ease-out (cubic-bezier(.16, 1, .3, 1)).
  const easeOut = (x: number) => 1 - Math.pow(1 - x, 4);

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.hero-scrub').forEach((figure) => {
    const reduceMotion = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
    const noFinePointer = matchMedia('(hover: none), (pointer: coarse)').matches;
    // Still visitors get frame 0 alone (the small hero-idle.webp, not the
    // sprite) drawn once into the same canvas, so the night light reaches
    // them too. The <img> stays as the fallback if the canvas fails.
    const still = reduceMotion || noFinePointer;

    const canvas = figure.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('.hero-scrub__canvas')!;
    // The sprite is matted (transparent backdrop), so the canvas needs
    // alpha; clearRect each frame leaves nothing behind.
    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d', { alpha: true });
    // The night light is built on a second canvas, clipped to her shape,
    // then blended onto the first.
    const fxCanvas = document.createElement('canvas');
    const fx = fxCanvas.getContext('2d', { alpha: true });
    // Floor shadow and contact pools, behind her (CSS px, it's all blur).
    const ground = figure.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('.hero-scrub__ground')!;
    const gctx = ground.getContext('2d');
    const silCanvas = document.createElement('canvas');
    const sil = silCanvas.getContext('2d');
    const tmpCanvas = document.createElement('canvas');
    const tmp = tmpCanvas.getContext('2d');
    const lightCanvas = document.createElement('canvas');
    const lctx = lightCanvas.getContext('2d');
    if (!ctx || !fx || !gctx || !sil || !tmp || !lctx) {
      figure.classList.add('no-js-scrub');
      return;
    }
    // The sprite is a grid; smoothing can bleed colour across a cell's
    // edge from its neighbour when scaled. Nearest-neighbour sampling
    // reads each cell exactly.
    ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = false;
    fx.imageSmoothingEnabled = false;

    const sprite = new Image();
    sprite.src = still ? '/images/hero-idle.webp' : '/images/hero-sprite.webp';

    let ready = false;
    let targetIndex = 0;
    let currentIndex = 0;
    let raf = 0;
    let lastFrame = -1;
    let drawnFrame = -1;
    let dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);
    let night = readNight();
    // How lit she is right now, 0-1. Starts at the page's mode, then
    // eases towards it when the theme changes.
    let lit = night.on;
    let fadeRaf = 0;
    let lk = readLampK();
    // Where the cursor lamp is (viewport px), from its `cursor-lamp` event.
    let lamp = { x: 0, y: 0, on: false, radius: 0 };
    let lampDirty = false;
    // Whether the lamp reached her (or her shadow) on the last paint, so
    // a lamp moving away still gets one repaint to clear its light.
    let lampWasNear = false;
    const lampNear = () => {
      if (!lamp.on) return false;
      const r = figure.getBoundingClientRect();
      const m = lamp.radius * lk.reach + r.width * 0.6;
      return lamp.x > r.left - m && lamp.x < r.right + m && lamp.y > r.top - m && lamp.y < r.bottom + m;
    };

    const sizeCanvas = () => {
      dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);
      const rect = figure.getBoundingClientRect();
      canvas.width = fxCanvas.width = Math.round(rect.width * dpr);
      canvas.height = fxCanvas.height = Math.round(rect.height * dpr);
      fx.imageSmoothingEnabled = ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = false;
      const gr = ground.getBoundingClientRect();
      ground.width = tmpCanvas.width = lightCanvas.width = Math.round(gr.width);
      ground.height = tmpCanvas.height = lightCanvas.height = Math.round(gr.height);
      silCanvas.width = Math.round(rect.width);
      silCanvas.height = Math.round(rect.height);
      drawnFrame = -1;
    };

    const W = () => canvas.width;
    const H = () => canvas.height;

    // Paints ellipses into fx, then keeps only what falls on her (her
    // frame's alpha), and blends the result onto the main canvas.
    const layer = (frameArgs: [number, number], mode: GlobalCompositeOperation, rgb: string, ellipses: Ellipse[], fillOuter = false) => {
      fx.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-over';
      fx.clearRect(0, 0, W(), H());
      for (const e of ellipses) {
        fx.save();
        fx.translate((e.cx / 100) * W(), (e.cy / 100) * H());
        fx.scale((e.rx / 100) * W(), (e.ry / 100) * H());
        const g = fx.createRadialGradient(0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1);
        // Alpha-only stops on one colour, so the fade doesn't pass
        // through black the way 'transparent' would.
        g.addColorStop(0, `rgb(${rgb} / ${Math.min(1, e.inner)})`);
        if (e.hold) g.addColorStop(e.hold, `rgb(${rgb} / ${Math.min(1, e.inner)})`);
        g.addColorStop(1, `rgb(${rgb} / ${Math.min(1, e.outer)})`);
        fx.fillStyle = g;
        // The shade keeps its rim value out to the frame's edges.
        if (fillOuter) fx.fillRect(-100, -100, 200, 200);
        else fx.fillRect(-1, -1, 2, 2);
        fx.restore();
      }
      fx.globalCompositeOperation = 'destination-in';
      fx.drawImage(sprite, frameArgs[0], frameArgs[1], CROP_W, CROP_H, 0, 0, W(), H());
      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = mode;
      ctx.drawImage(fxCanvas, 0, 0);
      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-over';
    };

    const light = (frame: number, src: [number, number]) => {
      if (lit <= 0) return;
      const { screen, shade } = night;
      const k = night.screenK * lit;
      const glowK = night.glowK * lit;
      const shadeK = night.shadeK * lit;
      const dx = FACE_DX[frame] ?? 0;
      const dy = FACE_DY[frame] ?? 0;
      // Shade: dark everywhere but a clear core where the screen lands
      // (half-following her head, since the core also covers her chest).
      if (shadeK > 0) {
        layer(src, 'multiply', shade, [{ cx: 45 + dx / 2, cy: 31 + dy / 2, rx: 20, ry: 15, inner: 0, hold: 0.25, outer: shadeK }], true);
      }
      // Screen light rising from the lid: chest (fixed), chin and lower
      // face, cheeks (following her head), the keyboard hand (fixed).
      if (k > 0) {
        layer(src, 'soft-light', screen, [
          { cx: 46, cy: 39, rx: 30, ry: 20, inner: 0.75 * k, outer: 0 },
          { cx: 45 + dx, cy: 25 + dy, rx: 15, ry: 8, inner: 0.85 * k, outer: 0 },
          { cx: 45 + dx, cy: 22 + dy, rx: 22, ry: 10, inner: 0.55 * k, outer: 0 },
          { cx: 33, cy: 48, rx: 8, ry: 4.5, inner: 0.75 * k, outer: 0 },
        ]);
      }
      if (glowK > 0) {
        layer(src, 'screen', screen, [{ cx: 45 + dx, cy: 25 + dy, rx: 14, ry: 7, inner: glowK, outer: 0 }]);
      }
    };

    // The lamp in this canvas's pixels, and how strongly it's on.
    const lampHere = () => {
      const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
      const s = r.width > 0 ? W() / r.width : 1;
      const reach = lamp.radius * lk.reach * s;
      const x = (lamp.x - r.left) * s, y = (lamp.y - r.top) * s;
      // Distance from the lamp to the nearest point of her box.
      const nx = Math.max(0, Math.min(W(), x)), ny = Math.max(0, Math.min(H(), y));
      const near = Math.hypot(x - nx, y - ny) < reach;
      return { x, y, reach, s, amt: lamp.on && near ? lit : 0 };
    };

    const frameAt = (c: CanvasRenderingContext2D, src: [number, number], dx = 0, dy = 0) =>
      c.drawImage(sprite, src[0], src[1], CROP_W, CROP_H, dx, dy, W(), H());

    const lampLight = (src: [number, number]) => {
      const L = lampHere();
      if (L.amt <= 0) return;
      const { hue } = lk;
      const cx = W() * 0.5, cy = H() * 0.45;
      const dx = cx - L.x, dy = cy - L.y, d = Math.hypot(dx, dy) || 1;

      // Form shade: the side away from the lamp dims.
      const nearK = Math.max(0, 1 - d / (L.reach * 1.6));
      if (lk.formK > 0 && nearK > 0) {
        const half = W() * 0.5;
        const g = ctx.createLinearGradient(cx - dx / d * half, cy - dy / d * half, cx + dx / d * half, cy + dy / d * half);
        g.addColorStop(0, `rgb(${night.shade} / 0)`);
        g.addColorStop(0.5, `rgb(${night.shade} / 0)`);
        g.addColorStop(1, `rgb(${night.shade} / ${lk.formK * nearK * L.amt})`);
        ctx.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-atop';
        ctx.fillStyle = g; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W(), H());
      }

      // Colour x light: a light map on black, times her colours, added.
      // On its own that brightens light colours most and near-black ones
      // not at all: her skin went orange and her pupils read as black
      // holes. So the added light is desaturated (--hero-lamp-sat) and
      // carries a small even lift (--hero-lamp-lift) that reaches the
      // darks too, the way a soft lamp fills an eye.
      fx.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-over';
      fx.fillStyle = '#000'; fx.fillRect(0, 0, W(), H());
      fx.globalCompositeOperation = 'lighter';
      fx.fillStyle = pool(fx, L.x, L.y, L.reach, hue, lk.gain * L.amt); fx.fillRect(0, 0, W(), H());
      fx.globalCompositeOperation = 'multiply'; frameAt(fx, src);
      if (lk.lift > 0) {
        fx.globalCompositeOperation = 'lighter';
        fx.fillStyle = pool(fx, L.x, L.y, L.reach, hue, lk.lift * L.amt); fx.fillRect(0, 0, W(), H());
      }
      fx.globalCompositeOperation = 'destination-in'; frameAt(fx, src);
      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = 'lighter';
      ctx.filter = `saturate(${lk.sat})`;
      ctx.drawImage(fxCanvas, 0, 0);
      ctx.filter = 'none';

      // Rim: her edge facing the lamp, lit by its pool. Fades out when
      // the lamp is over her, where there's no edge to face it.
      const over = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (d - W() * 0.15) / (W() * 0.35)));
      if (lk.rimK > 0 && over > 0) {
        const w = lk.rimW * L.s;
        fx.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-over';
        fx.clearRect(0, 0, W(), H());
        frameAt(fx, src);
        fx.globalCompositeOperation = 'destination-out'; frameAt(fx, src, dx / d * w, dy / d * w);
        fx.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-in';
        fx.fillStyle = pool(fx, L.x, L.y, L.reach * 1.15, hue, lk.rimK * L.amt * over); fx.fillRect(0, 0, W(), H());
        ctx.globalCompositeOperation = 'lighter'; ctx.drawImage(fxCanvas, 0, 0);
      }

      // Glint on the laptop lid, nudged toward the lamp.
      if (lk.glintK > 0) {
        const pts = LID.map(([x, y]) => [x / FRAME_W * W(), y / FRAME_H * H()]);
        const lx = pts.reduce((a, p) => a + p[0], 0) / 4, ly = pts.reduce((a, p) => a + p[1], 0) / 4;
        const amt = falloffAt(Math.hypot(L.x - lx, L.y - ly) / L.reach) * lk.glintK * L.amt;
        if (amt > 0.005) {
          const gx = lx + (L.x - lx) * 0.12, gy = ly + (L.y - ly) * 0.08;
          ctx.save();
          ctx.beginPath(); pts.forEach(([x, y], i) => (i ? ctx.lineTo(x, y) : ctx.moveTo(x, y))); ctx.closePath(); ctx.clip();
          const g = ctx.createRadialGradient(gx, gy, 0, gx, gy, W() * 0.16);
          g.addColorStop(0, `rgb(255 240 225 / ${amt})`); g.addColorStop(1, 'rgb(255 240 225 / 0)');
          ctx.globalCompositeOperation = 'screen'; ctx.fillStyle = g; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W(), H());
          ctx.restore();
        }
      }
      ctx.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-over';
    };

    // Behind her: contact pools (all night) and the floor shadow (only
    // in the lamp's light). In the ground canvas's CSS px; her box sits
    // at (bx, by) inside it.
    const drawGround = (src: [number, number], frameChanged: boolean) => {
      const GW = ground.width, GH = ground.height;
      gctx.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0);
      gctx.clearRect(0, 0, GW, GH);
      if (lit <= 0 || GW === 0) return;
      const fr = figure.getBoundingClientRect(), gr = ground.getBoundingClientRect();
      const bx = fr.left - gr.left, by = fr.top - gr.top, fw = fr.width, fh = fr.height;
      if (frameChanged) {
        sil.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-over';
        sil.clearRect(0, 0, silCanvas.width, silCanvas.height);
        sil.drawImage(sprite, src[0], src[1], CROP_W, CROP_H, 0, 0, silCanvas.width, silCanvas.height);
        sil.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-in';
        sil.fillStyle = '#000'; sil.fillRect(0, 0, silCanvas.width, silCanvas.height);
      }
      const y0 = by + fh * 0.988;   // the floor: her chair legs and slippers

      // The lamp's light on the floor around her, with her shadow cut out
      // of it. The page lamp alone is too faint on this ground for a
      // shadow to show (a shadow can only take away light that's there),
      // so the floor near her gets a little more, faded out well inside
      // this canvas's edges. Floor shadow: a point z above the floor moves
      // sideways by z * (base - lamp) / lampHeight, and back (up the
      // screen) by z * depth / lampHeight; it fades from the legs to the
      // tip and only exists where this light falls.
      if (lampNear() && lk.floorK > 0) {
        const lx = lamp.x - gr.left, ly = lamp.y - gr.top;
        // Wider than the page lamp's pool: the floor is lit at a grazing
        // angle, and a shadow needs light around it to read.
        const reach = lamp.radius * lk.reach * 1.8;
        lctx.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0);
        lctx.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-over';
        lctx.clearRect(0, 0, GW, GH);
        lctx.fillStyle = pool(lctx, lx, ly, reach, lk.hue, lk.floorK * lit);
        lctx.fillRect(0, 0, GW, GH);
        if (lk.castK > 0) {
          const cx = bx + fw / 2;
          const h = Math.max(y0 - ly, 30);
          const a = Math.max(-2.2, Math.min(2.2, (cx - lx) / h));
          const b = Math.max(0.06, Math.min(0.75, (fh * 0.2) / h));
          tmp.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-over';
          tmp.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0);
          tmp.clearRect(0, 0, GW, GH);
          tmp.filter = `blur(${Math.max(3, fh * 0.012)}px)`;
          tmp.setTransform(1, 0, -a, b, a * y0, y0 * (1 - b));
          tmp.drawImage(silCanvas, bx, by, fw, fh);
          tmp.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0);
          tmp.filter = 'none';
          const tx = cx + a * fh, ty = y0 - b * fh;
          const m = tmp.createLinearGradient(cx, y0, tx, ty);
          m.addColorStop(0, 'rgb(0 0 0 / 1)'); m.addColorStop(0.55, 'rgb(0 0 0 / 0.6)'); m.addColorStop(1, 'rgb(0 0 0 / 0)');
          tmp.globalCompositeOperation = 'destination-in';
          tmp.fillStyle = m; tmp.fillRect(0, 0, GW, GH);
          tmp.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-over';
          lctx.globalCompositeOperation = 'destination-out';
          lctx.globalAlpha = lk.castK;
          lctx.drawImage(tmpCanvas, 0, 0);
          lctx.globalAlpha = 1;
        }
        // Fade to nothing before this canvas's edges (an ellipse touching
        // all four sides, so even the corners are clear), so the extra
        // light never shows a cut line, wherever the lamp is.
        lctx.globalCompositeOperation = 'destination-in';
        lctx.save();
        lctx.translate(GW / 2, GH / 2);
        lctx.scale(GW / 2, GH / 2);
        const v = lctx.createRadialGradient(0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1);
        v.addColorStop(0, 'rgb(0 0 0 / 1)'); v.addColorStop(0.5, 'rgb(0 0 0 / 1)'); v.addColorStop(0.95, 'rgb(0 0 0 / 0)');
        lctx.fillStyle = v; lctx.fillRect(-1, -1, 2, 2);
        lctx.restore();
        lctx.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-over';
        gctx.drawImage(lightCanvas, 0, 0);
      }

      // Contact: her silhouette nudged down and blurred, kept only at the
      // feet. All night, lamp or not.
      if (lk.contactK > 0) {
        tmp.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0);
        tmp.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-over';
        tmp.clearRect(0, 0, GW, GH);
        tmp.filter = `blur(${Math.max(2, fh * 0.009)}px)`;
        tmp.drawImage(silCanvas, bx - fw * 0.03, by + fh * 0.012, fw * 1.06, fh);
        tmp.filter = 'none';
        const m = tmp.createLinearGradient(0, by + fh * 0.8, 0, y0 + fh * 0.02);
        m.addColorStop(0, 'rgb(0 0 0 / 0)'); m.addColorStop(0.75, 'rgb(0 0 0 / 1)'); m.addColorStop(1, 'rgb(0 0 0 / 0.6)');
        tmp.globalCompositeOperation = 'destination-in';
        tmp.fillStyle = m; tmp.fillRect(0, 0, GW, GH);
        tmp.globalCompositeOperation = 'source-over';
        gctx.globalAlpha = lk.contactK * lit;
        gctx.drawImage(tmpCanvas, 0, 0);
        gctx.globalAlpha = 1;
      }
    };

    const draw = (index: number) => {
      if (!ready || canvas.width === 0) return;
      const frame = still ? 0 : Math.max(0, Math.min(FRAME_COUNT - 1, Math.round(index)));
      if (frame !== lastFrame) {
        lastFrame = frame;
        figure.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('hero-scrub:frame', { detail: { frame, count: FRAME_COUNT }, bubbles: true }));
      }
      // Only repaint when the picture changes: a new frame, a resize, a
      // theme switch (which resets drawnFrame) or the lamp moving.
      if (frame === drawnFrame && !lampDirty) return;
      const frameChanged = frame !== drawnFrame;
      drawnFrame = frame;
      lampDirty = false;
      const src: [number, number] = still ? [0, 0] : [(frame % COLS) * FRAME_W + CROP_X, Math.floor(frame / COLS) * FRAME_H + CROP_Y];
      // Box aspect matches the frame (5:7), so it maps straight onto the
      // canvas. Clear first so no previous frame shows through.
      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);
      ctx.drawImage(sprite, src[0], src[1], CROP_W, CROP_H, 0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);
      light(frame, src);
      lampLight(src);
      drawGround(src, frameChanged);
      lampWasNear = lampNear();
    };

    sprite.decode().then(() => {
      ready = true;
      sizeCanvas();
      draw(0);
    }).catch(() => {
      figure.classList.add('no-js-scrub');
    });

    // The theme button flips data-mode on <html>; re-read the night
    // light's tokens and ease `lit` to the new mode over --dur-night, in
    // step with the CSS layers behind her (index.astro). Instant under
    // reduced motion.
    new MutationObserver(() => {
      night = readNight();
      lk = readLampK();
      cancelAnimationFrame(fadeRaf);
      const from = lit;
      const to = night.on;
      if (reduceMotion || night.ms <= 0 || from === to) {
        lit = to; drawnFrame = -1; draw(currentIndex);
        return;
      }
      const start = performance.now();
      const step = (now: number) => {
        const p = Math.min(1, (now - start) / night.ms);
        lit = from + (to - from) * easeOut(p);
        drawnFrame = -1; draw(currentIndex);
        if (p < 1) fadeRaf = requestAnimationFrame(step);
      };
      fadeRaf = requestAnimationFrame(step);
    }).observe(document.documentElement, { attributes: true, attributeFilter: ['data-mode'] });
    window.addEventListener('resize', () => { sizeCanvas(); draw(currentIndex); });

    // The lamp moved (or the page moved under it): repaint if it lights
    // her now, or did last time and needs clearing. The ground canvas
    // also repaints for the floor shadow.
    addEventListener('cursor-lamp', (e) => {
      lamp = (e as CustomEvent<typeof lamp>).detail;
      if (lit <= 0 || (!lampNear() && !lampWasNear)) return;
      lampDirty = true;
      if (still) draw(0);
    });
    addEventListener('scroll', () => {
      if (lit > 0 && (lampNear() || lampWasNear)) lampDirty = true;
    }, { passive: true });

    if (still) return;

    const tick = () => {
      currentIndex += (targetIndex - currentIndex) * SMOOTHING;
      if (Math.abs(targetIndex - currentIndex) < 0.01) currentIndex = targetIndex;
      draw(currentIndex);
      raf = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
    };
    raf = requestAnimationFrame(tick);

    const setTargetFromPointer = (x: number, y: number, width: number, height: number) => {
      const nx = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, width > 0 ? x / width : 0));
      const ny = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, height > 0 ? y / height : 0));
      const blended = nx * (1 - Y_INFLUENCE) + ny * Y_INFLUENCE;
      targetIndex = blended * (FRAME_COUNT - 1);
    };

    // The pointer is read over the whole band the figure sits in (the
    // hero), and its position across that band sets the frame, so she
    // follows the cursor from anywhere in the hero, not only over her own
    // box (where the full clip was squeezed into a few hundred pixels).
    const area = figure.closest<HTMLElement>('[data-themeband]') ?? figure;
    const onMove = (e: PointerEvent) => {
      const r = area.getBoundingClientRect();
      setTargetFromPointer(e.clientX - r.left, e.clientY - r.top, r.width, r.height);
    };
    const onLeave = () => { targetIndex = 0; };

    area.addEventListener('pointerenter', onMove);
    area.addEventListener('pointermove', onMove);
    area.addEventListener('pointerleave', onLeave);
    figure.addEventListener('focus', () => { targetIndex = (FRAME_COUNT - 1) * 0.72; });
    figure.addEventListener('blur', onLeave);

    window.addEventListener('beforeunload', () => cancelAnimationFrame(raf));
  });
</script>
